{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297, primary git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4243728e3cfdac5485f526d868c49aa5074f242e, implementation request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:59154b8746afa9148f9c48026b269b6fdaabc8b1 and promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c2c186516fa6f2df92a9b2d23f605c5bf744c388. I read the complete request, primary report, all fourteen changed paths and author gate/mutation evidence, the adopted proposal ddaf3197 and ratification ecc3db6f, Planner's original findings, adoption reconciliation 754296bb and census ed87935e. Ordinary inherited staleness is acknowledged. I have also read and incorporate the later finding git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c31754cf1152e84076518f42867e7594f58e2f4a.\n\nRequired correction: internal/app/app.go:1995 skips the unsigned size check when config.PayloadCeiling is zero. That supported legacy/attached path still signs an oversized act, contrary to the adopted before-signing condition. The small-act-only fallback test does not test that condition. This is not a claim that kernel admission accepts oversized events.\n\nIndependent reproducible evidence on this exact head, Go 1.26.7, in my detached checkout and disposable synthetic repositories:\n1. Start with TestSignRequestRefusesOverCeilingBeforeSigning. After Init's 2048-byte genesis, clone/save the isolated configuration with PayloadCeiling=0, reopen it with Open, reinstall the existing signatureCounter, then perform its same 4096-byte evidence Act. The kernel returns the expected ceiling refusal; the intended zero-signature assertion fails: 'the refused act was signed 1 time(s)' (1.471s package run).\n2. A separate probe uses real AttachConfig. Init a source at ceiling 2048, fetch its refs/seq/\u003cgenesis\u003e into a new testRepo, AttachConfig that repository with the source genesis/object format, and pass the synthetic source actor's private key to attached.BuildActRequest for an assert carrying 4096 evidence bytes. AttachConfig records ceiling zero. BuildActRequest succeeds, intent.Verify confirms its returned signature, and the signature observer is exactly one. source.AcceptSubmission then refuses with the genesis ceiling error. The probe fails on the missing before-signing boundary (1.651s package run). No real workroom key/configuration/resident was changed.\nThe probes are retained at /tmp/git22397-legacy-probe.go and /tmp/git22397-attached-probe.go with their matching .txt output and overlay JSON. The initial /var overlay did not select the test and an initial in-memory-only legacy alteration hit the immutable-config consistency guard; neither is counted as the counterexample. The final runs used canonical paths and, for legacy, saved/reopened synthetic configuration.\n\nObtain the authoritative ceiling before signing when the local field is absent; preserve shared kernel accounting, final kernel enforcement, ordinary small acts and exact accepted-retry behavior. Add actual oversized legacy and attached controls observing zero signatures and no append, with admitted controls proving the observer works. Do not replace the skip with a blanket zero-ceiling refusal. Correct the architecture and limits wording to agree with the delivered adopted boundary. This satisfies the existing outcome and stays on c2c18651; no new implementation outcome or adoption is needed. A deliberate weaker boundary would require Hugh's actual revised adoption, as the existing reconciliation states.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are 2 (kernel/intent accounting) and 7 (application request authoring, CLI/MCP/resident and documentation). The same-head architecture amendment is present and its exported shared-accounting description is sound. Its no-local-ceiling exception changes the adopted contract, while limits.md still claims before-signing coverage everywhere; approval requires resolving that inconsistency through the correction above. No locator, schema/profile change or transport-cap change is delivered.\n\nSecurity: final genesis enforcement, fixed-width Ed25519 envelope measurement, bounded quoted attachment-name diagnostics and overflow refusal are preserved in the examined paths. I checked the 32-byte public key guard, 64-byte placeholder signature and RawURL base64 fixed-length envelope, saturating addition and remaining-budget short-circuit arithmetic. Both signatures use the already encoded intent bytes; SignEncoded still validates signing bytes. No secret material or automatic locator access is introduced. The unresolved signing-boundary defect above is the reason to request changes. Ordinary proposal plus Hugh's ratification governs this work, not a newly inferred authority-bearing request chain.\n\nSimplification: retain the one shared unsigned measurement at signRequest and the common kernel judgement; per-surface duplicate checks are unnecessary. I independently confirmed cmd/gs/main.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and internal/service/ui.go are byte-identical to d1ae6ade. The corrected census is clearly attributed, separates rooms, and withdraws the zero-refusal and historical-slope inferences; no new census run is needed for this correction.\n\nValidation: my focused delivered tests passed in kernel (0.661s), app (1.674s), gs (2.088s), MCP (2.802s) and service (2.370s), including ordinary-ceiling signature/no-append and accepted-small-act controls. A separate full internal/intent run passed (0.282s); the initial multi-package selection had selected no intent tests and is not counted as intent coverage. Diff whitespace checks passed. The author's full package/race/docset/build/vet and thirteen final red omission controls remain attributed evidence, including the two earlier mutant survivals and their fixes. I did not rerun the whole module or all thirteen mutants. Correct on the live implementation promise, publish the new exact head and reporting artifact citing this review, then request fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4243728e3cfdac5485f526d868c49aa5074f242e","binding":"assigned","head":"e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ee37c9f517b6932273a27c1f88b3f7c21f876544\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c31754cf1152e84076518f42867e7594f58e2f4a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c2c186516fa6f2df92a9b2d23f605c5bf744c388\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c31754cf1152e84076518f42867e7594f58e2f4a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4243728e3cfdac5485f526d868c49aa5074f242e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:49846f737a726a4c9bb50db06e7e65d841d41ba7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c31754cf1152e84076518f42867e7594f58e2f4a, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ee37c9f517b6932273a27c1f88b3f7c21f876544 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3acec403ed0d43bcd2a3c38bd188f7740ef and 211 more","staleness":"artifact, promise, request stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3a